Implemented with optional shading. Also note that this was implemented for Apple
Silicon Mac so may have to tweak for other platforms.

To run, first do `make all`
Then run `./geometry [path/to/scene.txt] [xres] [yres] [h] [shading_type]`
with shading_type being an optional parameter to turn Phong shading on. Any
value will work.

For my implementation of F:
To create F, we first start with the identity by setting diagonals to 1.
We then set all the non diagonal entries to be the summation of the cotangents.

To calculate the cotangents, we just create two vectors on the edges according
to Figure 6 from the Lecture Notes. Taking the dot product, we can get the
cosine and taking the cross product we can get the sine.

For a vertex i and column j, where i != j, they sum to the first term of the
summation but we have to still account for the j counts of the second term of
the summation (the x_i term). We store it in the diagonal entry of the matrix by
subtracting it. Also because this second term in the summation is negative, we
subtract the sum.
